  "walletUpgradeReview": {
    "from": "2e73db164965bd3cf879f80f24101901a76bc72f",
    "to": "HEAD of lygos/one-parser-1 (including this record and subsequent manifest-only bookkeeping)",
    "sourceEvidence": "Wallet SOURCE.json; Linux report ONE-PARSER-ENGINE-BUILD-20261105 reproduces shipped wasm 7cf71bd212d07295d0499d88218b22460ee2c03879ec159c372dce5895216a57 from this source.",
    "notTheShippedBase": "43cbee38 builds b8d1b7f5748ee99b74b4d79108c34b83353aef7eed9b5edabc8b811fcd13088d; its WASM-SHA256 is stale.",
    "summary": [
      {
        "class": "A+B",
        "area": "Bitcoin parser inherited from upstream #600 and follow-ups",
        "changes": [
          "BIP-174 redeem-script, witness-script and witness-only input validation runs before recognition. Invalid claimed bare inputs now refuse instead of receiving a display.",
          "Taproot inputs with only claimed amounts now show a claimed fee enforced by BIP-341 signature, rather than Verified. Six taproot golden displays change accordingly.",
          "BIP vectors, recorded mainnet fixtures and optional live regtest coverage are added; recognizer tests reflect the input validation and the reserved literal-label count increases 25 to 26."
        ]
      },
      {
        "class": "B+C",
        "area": "Wallet-payment policy and change labels",
        "changes": [
          "New wallet-payment policy reuses strict verified-input/signed-data withdrawal checks; ordinary none and vault-withdrawal retain bare-only recognition.",
          "Only the exact Your change label on owned P2PKH, P2SH, P2WPKH, P2WSH or P2TR scripts enters the explicit output allow-list. Inputs and unlisted address outputs are never queried; full destination addresses remain in previews and fallback text. Future witness programs and bare change labels refuse.",
          "Owned scripts still match exact bytes. Duplicate scripts and duplicate vault numbers refuse; multiple distinct change scripts are allowed. A value constructed under wallet-payment cannot be reused under another policy.",
          "Six original Bitcoin contract tests are unchanged by this repair; new display matrix covers five standard forms, unlisted outputs, policy isolation and label/type refusals."
        ]
      },
      {
        "class": "D",
        "area": "Display engine and checks",
        "changes": [
          "Engine and lockfile identity move from display-core/0.1.0 to display-core/0.2.0, changing engine-bound digests even for identical payloads. Digest test checks same-engine equality and 0.1.0 inequality.",
          "Wallet-payment string boundary and rules are added; native expected counts become owned 29 and display-core 12; golden runner expects the new engine.",
          "Reported formatting diffs applied manually. WASM-SHA256, wallet artifacts and LINKED-CRATES.txt are deliberately not repinned before Linux execution and independent review.",
          "Fork classification and append-only change manifest record the source changes. The pre-existing manifest checker mismatch after upstream sync is still unresolved."
        ]
      },
      {
        "class": "upstream",
        "area": "Shared libraries reachable by display-core",
        "changes": [
          "visualsign adds reversible free-form text/byte escaping and a Zcash registry variant. Generated protobuf types/descriptor add a Zcash chain variant and Solana max_fee_lamports with number-or-string serde support.",
          "The isolated display-core dependency lock differs from shipped source only in its own version; shared path-crate source has nevertheless changed and must be reviewed. Linux chain-isolation and wasm checks must be rerun."
        ]
      },
      {
        "class": "upstream",
        "area": "Inherited repository changes outside the Bitcoin wasm path",
        "changes": [
          "Upstream sync through 64b3d792 includes Solana fee caps/compute-budget accounting, split Anza dependencies, off-chain message rendering, Token-2022 decoding, SWIG discriminator display, associated-token and other preset changes.",
          "Sui migrates decoding to sui-sdk-types and updates Fluid deployments and rendering/tests; NEAR rejects noncanonical Borsh and gains intent changes; intents are extracted into a separate crate with display changes.",
          "Zcash keyless PCZT parser, fixtures and chain wiring are added. Ethereum Permit2 rendering fixes, property/fuzz tests and recorded mainnet coverage are added.",
          "Workspace dependency locks, CLI/parser/integration/host/codegen wiring, protobuf schema, docs, CI/security/lint and deploy-tool dependencies change. These repository changes are not evidence that another chain is linked into the Bitcoin wasm; linked path-source changes are separately listed above."
        ]
      }
    ],
